{
  "slug": "shortcut",
  "name": "Shortcut",
  "aliases": [
    "Clubhouse",
    "Shortcut.com"
  ],
  "description": "Let your AI work in Shortcut: search stories with Shortcut's search operators, read stories with tasks, comments and history, epics, iterations, objectives, teams, workflows and labels, and create, update and comment on stories after you confirm. Personal API token.",
  "instructions": "## Shortcut\nThis connector works with **Shortcut** (formerly Clubhouse), the project management tool for software teams, through the official **REST API v3** (`https://api.app.shortcut.com/api/v3`). It reads stories, epics, iterations, objectives, teams, workflows, labels and members, searches stories with Shortcut's search operators, reads a story's change history, and can create and update stories and add comments.\n\n**Setup (about 2 minutes)**\n1. In Shortcut, click your avatar, then **Settings**, **Your Account**, **API Tokens** (https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens).\n2. Enter a name such as AnythingMCP and click **Generate Token**. Shortcut shows the token once.\n3. Paste it into `SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN`, install, and run `shortcut_get_current_member`.\n\n**Whose rights**: the token acts as you, in the workspace it was created in, with your permissions. Stories, comments and changes made through this connector appear under your name. A workspace with several organizations needs one token per workspace.\n\n**Writes: confirm first.** `shortcut_create_story`, `shortcut_update_story` and `shortcut_add_story_comment` change the workspace at once and notify followers. Show the user what will be created or changed (story, fields, comment text) and wait for a clear yes before calling. `shortcut_delete_story` is installed switched off: deleting a story cannot be undone; archiving it with `shortcut_update_story` (`archived: true`) is the safer choice.\n\n**How to work**\n1. `shortcut_get_current_member` tells you who you are (your `mention_name` for `owner:` searches) and the workspace's default workflow.\n2. Ids first: `shortcut_list_workflows` (workflow state ids for moving stories), `shortcut_list_teams`, `shortcut_list_members` (member UUIDs for owners), `shortcut_list_labels`, `shortcut_list_iterations`, `shortcut_list_epics`, `shortcut_list_objectives`, `shortcut_list_projects`.\n3. Find stories with `shortcut_search_stories`, then `shortcut_get_story` for the description, tasks, comments and links, and `shortcut_get_story_history` for who changed what. Stories of one epic or iteration: `shortcut_list_epic_stories`, `shortcut_list_iteration_stories`. Find epics by text with `shortcut_search_epics`; `shortcut_get_epic` reads one.\n4. Change things with `shortcut_create_story`, `shortcut_update_story` (move it by setting `workflow_state_id`) and `shortcut_add_story_comment`.\n\n**Search operators** (`query` of `shortcut_search_stories` and `shortcut_search_epics`): combine words and operators with spaces, quote values with spaces.\n- `owner:jane` and `requester:jane` (mention name without @), `team:\"Mobile\"`, `epic:\"Checkout redesign\"` or `epic:123`, `iteration:\"Sprint 12\"`, `label:\"customer\"`, `state:\"In Progress\"`, `type:bug` (feature, bug, chore), `estimate:3`, `id:123`, `project:\"Backend\"`, `objective:\"Q4\"`.\n- `is:started`, `is:unstarted`, `is:done`, `is:blocked`, `is:blocker`, `is:archived`, `is:overdue`; `has:owner`, `has:epic`, `has:deadline`, `has:comment`, `has:task`.\n- Dates: `created:2026-10-01..2026-10-15`, `updated:today`, `completed:yesterday`, `due:*..2026-10-31` (`*` is open-ended).\n- `title:\"login\"`, `description:\"timeout\"`, `comment:\"customer\"` search one field. Put `!` in front of an operator to exclude, e.g. `!is:done`.\n- Example: `owner:jane is:started !is:archived type:bug`.\n\n**Paging**: searches return 25 results by default (at most 250); when `next` is present, call again with `next` set to the token after `next=` in that value. Only the first 1000 matches can be paged through, so narrow the query instead. `shortcut_list_epics` pages with `page` while `next` is a number.\n\n**Ids**: stories, epics, iterations, objectives, labels, projects and workflow states have numeric ids; members and teams have UUIDs. Dates are ISO 8601 in UTC.\n\n**Rate limit**: 200 requests per minute per token; on 429 wait a minute.\n\n**Common errors**\n- 401: the token is wrong or was deleted. Generate a new one under Settings, API Tokens.\n- 404: the id does not exist in this workspace.\n- 400 or 422: a field value is not accepted, e.g. a workflow state id from another workflow; Shortcut says which in the message.\n\n**Out of scope**: deleting epics, iterations, labels or comments, documents (Docs), files and attachments, custom fields editing, story templates, webhooks and integrations, tasks and story links.",
  "region": "intl",
  "category": "project-management",
  "icon": "shortcut",
  "docsUrl": "https://developer.shortcut.com/api/rest/v3",
  "prerequisites": "A Shortcut account in the workspace you want to use, to create a personal API token under Settings, Your Account, API Tokens. About 2 minutes.",
  "appRegistrationUrl": "https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": {
      "label": "API token",
      "kind": "credential",
      "secret": true,
      "help": "Shortcut, Settings, Your Account, API Tokens, Generate Token. Shortcut shows it once. It acts as you in that workspace.",
      "link": "https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens",
      "example": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
      "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9-]{20,}$",
      "patternMessage": "Paste only the token: letters, digits and dashes, no spaces."
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Shortcut does not accept this token: it is wrong or was deleted. Generate a new one under Settings, Your Account, API Tokens.",
    "404": "Shortcut does not know this id in this workspace.",
    "429": "Shortcut allows 200 requests per minute per token. Wait a minute and try again."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "shortcut_get_current_member"
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Shortcut REST API v3",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.app.shortcut.com/api/v3",
    "authType": "API_KEY",
    "authConfig": {
      "headerName": "Shortcut-Token",
      "apiKey": "{{SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN}}"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json",
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "User-Agent": "AnythingMCP"
    },
    "healthcheckPath": "/member"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "shortcut_get_current_member",
      "description": "Read who the API token belongs to: member id (UUID), name, mention name (for owner: searches), role, and the workspace with its name, URL slug, default workflow id and point scale. Use it first to check the connection.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/member"
      },
      "responseMapping": {
        "transform": {
          "select": {
            "id": "$.id",
            "name": "$.name",
            "mention_name": "$.mention_name",
            "role": "$.role",
            "is_owner": "$.is_owner",
            "workspace": {
              "name": "$.workspace2.name",
              "url_slug": "$.workspace2.url_slug",
              "default_workflow_id": "$.workspace2.default_workflow_id",
              "estimate_scale": "$.workspace2.estimate_scale",
              "utc_offset": "$.workspace2.utc_offset"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "shortcut_list_members",
      "description": "List the members of the workspace: id (UUID, used for owner_ids and requested_by_id), name, mention name, role and whether they are disabled. E-mail addresses are left out. Active members only unless disabled is true.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "disabled": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "true lists only disabled members; default false lists active members.",
            "default": false
          }
        }
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/members",
        "queryParams": {
          "disabled": "$disabled"
        }
      },
      "responseMapping": {
        "transform": {
          "select": {
            "members": {
              "$from": "$[*]",
              "$select": {
                "id": "id",
                "name": "profile.name",
                "mention_name": "profile.mention_name",
                "role": "role",
                "state": "state",
                "disabled": "disabled",
                "group_ids": "group_ids"
              }
            }
          },
          "maxBytes": 60000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "shortcut_list_workflows",
      "description": "List the workflows of the workspace with their states: workflow id and name, default state, team, and each state's id, name, type (unstarted, started, done) and position. Use a state id as workflow_state_id to create or move a story.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
